# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is git-ignored and never committed.
#
# Nothing here is needed for Phases 0 to 2. The key is only used from Phase 3,
# and only inside the serverless AI function, never in the app itself.
# Leave it blank and the AI runs in MOCK mode.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# From Phase 5. Leave both out locally: with no GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID the app offers
# a clearly labelled test-mode sign-in, and accounts are kept in memory.
# On the live site these come from Google and from Upstash (connected through
# Vercel's Storage tab, which sets its two by itself).
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# From Phase 6, for the Pro plan. Leave all three out locally: with no Stripe
# keys, Settings offers a clearly labelled pretend upgrade so the flow can be
# tested without a card. That pretend upgrade is refused on the live site.
# All three or none: a half-configured Stripe would take a payment and never
# grant the plan. The secret key is a secret; the price id is not.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# STRIPE_PRICE_ID=
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# From Phase 7. Selling is switched off: every account gets the same generous
# AI ceiling and nothing in the app offers to take money. All the Stripe code
# is still there and still tested. Set this to 1 to bring the Pro offer back.
# ENABLE_PRO=
